  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "古文字專題",
    "sub_ename": "THESIS STUDY OF PALEOGRAPHY",
    "describe_ch": "漢字淵源流長，一直作為不斷記錄中華文化歷史的載体。近現代由於金石學、考古學的蓬勃發展，地下出土大量古代文字資料，加上自清儒以來倡導用文字破經史的考據方法，古文字的認識在文化史、學術史上有不可取代的價值。\n本課程重點講授漢字的發展歷史，自上古的岩畫始,經夏代的陶文、商代的甲骨文、兩周金文、春秋戰國的竹簡帛書，以迄秦漢的《說文》古文，提供同學對漢字一較全面認識和訓練，並掌握應用古文字了解古書和古文化的方法。",
    "describe_eh": "The origin and development of Chinese Characters have a long history, serving as a continuous record of Chinese cultural heritage. In recent times, with the flourishing development of epigraphy and archaeology, a large number of ancient textual materials have been unearthed. Since the Confucian scholars of the Qing Dynasty advocated the textual criticism method of interpreting classics and history, the understanding of ancient characters has held irreplaceable value in cultural and academic history.\nThis course focuses on the developmental history of Chinese characters, starting from ancient rock paintings, through the pottery inscriptions of the Xia Dynasty, the oracle bone inscriptions of the Shang Dynasty, the bronze inscriptions of the Eastern and Western Zhou dynasties, the bamboo and silk manuscripts of the Spring and Autumn period and the Warring States period, up to the ancient texts in the Origin of Chinese Characters (Shuowen Jiezi) of the Qin and Han dynasties. It provides students with a comprehensive understanding and training in Chinese characters and enables them to grasp the methods of using ancient characters to understand ancient texts and cultures.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
